\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\kerning2\b\f0\fs20\lang16393 Agentic AI\par
\b0 As Artificial Intelligence evolves, we are moving from systems that simply \b respond to prompts\b0  toward systems that can \b reason, plan, make decisions, and take actions autonomously\b0 . This new paradigm is called \b Agentic AI\b0 .\par
In simple terms:\par
\b Agentic AI is an AI system that can perceive its environment, reason about goals, create plans, use tools, take actions, learn from outcomes, and work toward completing tasks with minimal human intervention.\b0\par
Unlike traditional AI applications that wait for instructions at every step, Agentic AI behaves more like a digital worker or assistant that can independently determine how to achieve an objective.\par
\par
\b Why Do We Need Agentic AI?\par
\b0 Traditional AI models such as GPT can generate text, answer questions, summarize documents, and write code. However, they have limitations:\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 They mostly react to prompts.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}They do not inherently manage long-term goals.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}They cannot continuously monitor environments.\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}They struggle with multi-step workflows without orchestration.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 For example:\par
\b Traditional AI\par
\b0 User:\par
"Book me the cheapest flight."\par
AI:\par
"Here are some flight options."\par
The AI provides information but cannot complete the entire workflow.\par
\b Agentic AI\par
\b0 User:\par
"Book me the cheapest flight to Bangalore next weekend."\par
Agent:\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent360\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Searches flight websites.\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}Compares prices.\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}Checks user preferences.\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}Selects the optimal route.\par
{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}Requests approval.\par
{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}Completes booking.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 The system not only thinks but also acts.\par
\par
\b What Makes an AI "Agentic"?\par
\b0 An AI agent possesses several important characteristics.\par
\b 1. Goal-Oriented Behavior\par
\b0 The agent focuses on accomplishing an objective rather than merely answering questions.\par
Example:\par
Goal:\par
Reduce cloud infrastructure costs by 15%.\par
Instead of generating a report, the agent:\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Analyzes utilization metrics\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Identifies wastage\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Proposes optimizations\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Simulates savings\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Creates implementation plans\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 2. Planning Capability\par
\b0 Agentic systems decompose large objectives into smaller manageable tasks.\par
\b Example\par
\b0 Goal:\par
Develop a customer support chatbot.\par
The AI may create a plan:\par
1. Gather requirements\par
2. Design architecture\par
3. Create intents\par
4. Build backend\par
5. Train models\par
6. Test workflows\par
7. Deploy application\par
This resembles human project planning.\par
\par
\b 3. Reasoning\par
\b0 Reasoning allows agents to evaluate alternatives and choose the best course of action.\par
Example:\par
Option A: Faster\par
Option B: Cheaper\par
Option C: More reliable\par
The agent evaluates trade-offs and selects the most suitable option according to objectives.\par
\par
\b 4. Tool Usage\par
\b0 One of the most important aspects of Agentic AI is the ability to use external tools.\par
Examples:\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Web Search\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Databases\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}APIs\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Email systems\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}ERP systems\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}CRM platforms\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Code interpreters\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}File systems\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Instead of relying solely on its training data, the agent can interact with the external world.\par
\par
\b 5. Memory\par
\b0 Agents maintain context over longer periods.\par
\b Short-Term Memory\par
\b0 Stores information during a conversation.\par
Example:\par
User lives in Kolkata.\par
Preferred airline is IndiGo.\par
Budget is \f1\u8377?\f0 10,000.\par
\b Long-Term Memory\par
\b0 Preserves information across interactions.\par
Example:\par
Past purchases\par
User preferences\par
Historical workflows\par
Business context\par
Memory enables personalized decision-making.\par
\par
\b 6. Reflection and Self-Correction\par
\b0 An advanced agent can review its own actions.\par
Workflow:\par
Act\par
\f2\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Observe\par
\f2\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Evaluate\par
\f2\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Correct\par
\f2\u8595?\f0\lang16393\par
Act again\par
This iterative improvement process significantly enhances reliability.\par
\par
