{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Databases and enterprise systems\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Web information\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Application logs\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Sensor or IoT data\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Images, audio, and video\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Example\par
\b0 Consider a financial leakage detection agent:\par
Inputs:\par
\bullet  ERP transaction records\par
\bullet  Vendor invoices\par
\bullet  Employee expense reports\par
\bullet  Audit logs\par
\~\par
The agent perceives:\par
\bullet  Duplicate payments\par
\bullet  Unusual transaction patterns\par
\bullet  Missing approvals\par
\bullet  Policy violations\par
\b Why Perception Matters\par
\b0 Without perception, an agent has no awareness of its environment. Accurate perception ensures that the agent's decisions are based on real and relevant information.\par
\par
\b 2. Reason\par
Reasoning\b0  is the ability to analyze information, draw conclusions, evaluate options, and make decisions.\par
Once the agent understands a situation, it must determine:\par

\pard{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf7\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 What is happening?\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Why is it happening?\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}What should be done next?\par
{\pntext\f7\'B7\tab}Which option is best?\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Reasoning transforms raw data into intelligent decisions.\par
\b Types of Reasoning\par
Logical Reasoning\par
\b0 Uses rules and logic.\par
Example:\par
If invoice amount > approval limit\par
AND approval is missing\par
\~\par
Then:\par
Flag transaction as non-compliant.\par
\b Analytical Reasoning\par
\b0 Finds patterns and relationships.\par
Example:\par
Multiple payments\par
\f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Same vendor\par
\f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Similar amount\par
\f2\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Short time interval\par
\~\par
Possible duplicate payment.\par
\b Strategic Reasoning\par
\b0 Evaluates multiple paths before choosing one.\par
Example:\par
Plain Text\par
Option A: Faster resolution\par
Option B: Lower cost\par
Option C: Lower risk\par
\~\par
Choose based on business goal.\par
\b Example\par
\b0 A customer service agent receives a complaint.\par
The agent reasons:\par
Plain Text\par
Customer sentiment = negative\par
Issue severity = high\par
Account value = premium\par
\~\par
Decision:\par
Route ticket to senior support team.\par
Reasoning is effectively the "brain" of an agentic system.\par
\par
\b 3. Act\par
Action\b0  is the ability to execute decisions and interact with the external world.\par
Traditional AI often stops after generating an answer.\par
Agentic AI goes further by taking action to achieve a goal.\par
